    "file": "references/formats.md",
    "title": "Formats",
    "body": "# Formats\n\nPage types that are not the marketing site, the app, or the shop. Those are `surfaces.md`, `narrative.md`, and `commerce.md`. The same directions and the same tokens apply. Only the job changes.\n\n## Portfolio and case study\n\nThe work comes first. A case study opens on the piece or the outcome, not on a portrait and a paragraph about passion.\n\nStructure:\n\n- The name of the work, as the `h1`.\n- One sentence on what it was.\n- The work, large, with captions.\n- Then, if you have them: the constraint, what you did, what changed. Specific. \"Cut the checkout from 4 steps to 2. Completion went from 41% to 63%.\" Not \"delivered a seamless experience.\"\n- Next work is one link at the end, not a grid that pulls the eye off the piece before it has been seen.\n\nA portfolio index is a directory (`layout.md`) or a simple list of names and years. The thumbnail is the work, cropped the same way each time. No mockup frames, no device bezels, unless the work is the device UI and the bezel is honest.\n\n## Event and launch\n\nOne date, one place or one link, one action. The date is typography, not a calendar widget. A launch page is a poster (`sense.md`) with the facts a person needs to decide: what, when, where, what it costs, how to come.\n\nA schedule is a list: time in `.num`, session name, one line, the room or the link. Not a colored grid of overlapping blocks unless the event is a conference and the overlap is the point. Then it is a tool, and it follows Spec.\n\nDo not count down unless the moment is real and the clock is accurate.\n\n## Help center\n\nA search field with a real label, then the six questions people actually have, as links in a list. Groups are nouns: Billing, Baking, Account. An article is Broadsheet or Civic: a title, the answer in the first paragraph, then the steps. Steps follow `information.md`.\n\nThe article does not open with a hero, a smile, and \"Welcome to the help center.\"\n\n## Changelog\n\nReverse chronological. The date, then a version if you have one, then bullets of what changed in the product's verbs. \"You can refund an order from the row.\" Not \"Refund flow improvements and various bug fixes.\"\n\nGroup a day's notes under one date. Do not card each bullet.\n\n## Status\n\nThe current state is a sentence at the top: \"All systems are up.\" or \"Checkout is down. We are on it.\" Color helps. The sentence works without it.\n\nBelow, a list of parts with a word for each (Up, Degraded, Down) and the time of the last change. An incident is a short log: time, what we know, what we are doing. No marketing.\n\n## Account\n\nThe person's name, the way they sign in, and the few settings that are about them rather than about the work. Work settings stay in the product (`surfaces.md`). This page is identity, email, password, and leaving.\n\nDestructive acts (delete account, leave the team) are last, in their own group, and they confirm with the dialog in `components.md`. Show what will be deleted in one sentence.\n\n## Inbox\n\nA list of messages as `.rows`: who, the first line, the time. Unread is weight, not a colored dot alone. Opening one shows the thread as a document, the reply at the end. Do not card each message. Do not put a face on every system event. Faces are for people.\n\n## Onboarding\n\nOne action that creates the first real object. The empty product in `surfaces.md` is this, and it is the whole first run. A second step is allowed only if the first object cannot exist without it.\n\nDo not tour the interface with a chain of modals. Do not explain a control that has a visible label. If a hint is required, it is one quiet line next to the thing, and it can be dismissed. After the first object exists, the hints go away. The person is in the product, not in a setup wizard wearing the product's colors.\n\n## Missing and down\n\n404, no matches, and outages are specified in `arrange.md`. They use this product's type and frame.\n\n## Auth-adjacent legal pages\n\nPrivacy, terms, and returns are documents. Set them as documents (`surfaces.md` docs): measure, real headings, the date they took effect at the top. Do not design them as marketing pages with illustrations. People came to read the obligation.",
